    "role": "user",
    "content": "Program: CBTRN02C. Input files and their record layouts:\n\nDALYTRAN: CVTRA06Y DALYTRAN-RECORD (350 bytes)\n  DALYTRAN-ID                  X(16)\n  DALYTRAN-TYPE-CD             X(2)\n  DALYTRAN-CAT-CD              9(4)\n  DALYTRAN-SOURCE              X(10)\n  DALYTRAN-DESC                X(100)\n  DALYTRAN-AMT                 S9(9)V9(2)\n  DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-ID         9(9)\n  DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-NAME       X(50)\n  DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-CITY       X(50)\n  DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-ZIP        X(10)\n  DALYTRAN-CARD-NUM            X(16)\n  DALYTRAN-ORIG-TS             X(26)\n  DALYTRAN-PROC-TS             X(26)\n\nXREF: CVACT03Y CARD-XREF-RECORD (50 bytes)\n  XREF-CARD-NUM                X(16)\n  XREF-CUST-ID                 9(9)\n  XREF-ACCT-ID                 9(11)\n\nACCOUNT: CVACT01Y ACCOUNT-RECORD (300 bytes)\n  ACCT-ID                      9(11)\n  ACCT-ACTIVE-STATUS           X(1)\n  ACCT-CURR-BAL                S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CREDIT-LIMIT            S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CASH-CREDIT-LIMIT       S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-OPEN-DATE               X(10)\n  ACCT-EXPIRAION-DATE          X(10)\n  ACCT-REISSUE-DATE            X(10)\n  ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT         S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT          S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-ADDR-ZIP                X(10)\n  ACCT-GROUP-ID                X(10)\n\nTCATBAL: CVTRA01Y TRAN-CAT-BAL-RECORD (50 bytes)\n  TRANCAT-ACCT-ID              9(11)\n  TRANCAT-TYPE-CD              X(2)\n  TRANCAT-CD                   9(4)\n  TRAN-CAT-BAL                 S9(9)V9(2)\n\nRule to test:\n{\n \"id\": \"BR-CBTRN02C-005\",\n \"title\": \"Route each daily transaction to posting or to the reject file, and set return code 4 when anything is rejected\",\n \"summary\": \"Each daily transaction record is validated. If the failure reason code is still 0, the transaction is posted. Otherwise the reject count goes up by one and a reject record is written, made of the full 350-byte daily record followed by an 80-byte trailer holding the reason code and its description. When the run ends, the program prints the processed and rejected counts and sets return code 4 if at least one transaction was rejected.\",\n \"given\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"For every daily transaction record read, the processed-transaction count goes up by 1. The failure reason code is reset to 0 and its description to spaces before validation runs.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"END-OF-FILE\",\n    \"WS-TRANSACTION-COUNT\",\n    \"WS-VALIDATION-FAIL-REASON\",\n    \"WS-VALIDATION-FAIL-REASON-DESC\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"N\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"A reject record is 430 bytes. It holds a 350-byte copy of the transaction data followed by an 80-byte validation trailer. The trailer is a 4-digit unsigned reason code followed by a 76-character reason description.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"REJECT-RECORD\",\n    \"REJECT-TRAN-DATA\",\n    \"VALIDATION-TRAILER\",\n    \"WS-VALIDATION-TRAILER\",\n    \"WS-VALIDATION-FAIL-REASON\",\n    \"WS-VALIDATION-FAIL-REASON-DESC\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  }\n ],\n \"when\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"After validation, the failure reason code decides what happens: 0 means the transaction is posted, and any other value means it is rejected.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-VALIDATION-FAIL-REASON\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"0\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"then\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"If the reason code is 0, the transaction is posted: the transaction-category balance is updated, then the account record, then the transaction file is written. The reject branch (reject count and reject record) is skipped for that transaction.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-VALIDATION-FAIL-REASON\",\n    \"WS-REJECT-COUNT\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"0\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"If the reason code is not 0, the reject count goes up by 1 and one reject record is written for that transaction.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-REJECT-COUNT\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The reject record holds the whole daily transaction record unchanged, followed by the trailer containing the current reason code and description. It is written to the daily rejects file.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"DALYTRAN-RECORD\",\n    \"REJECT-TRAN-DATA\",\n    \"WS-VALIDATION-TRAILER\",\n    \"VALIDATION-TRAILER\",\n    \"FD-REJS-RECORD\",\n    \"REJECT-RECORD\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"At the end of the run, the program prints the processed count and the rejected count with fixed labels.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-TRANSACTION-COUNT\",\n    \"WS-REJECT-COUNT\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"TRANSACTIONS PROCESSED :\",\n    \"TRANSACTIONS REJECTED  :\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"If at least one transaction was rejected, the program ends with return code 4. Otherwise the return code is left unchanged.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-REJECT-COUNT\",\n    \"RETURN-CODE\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"4\"\n   ]\n  }\n ]\n}"
